      "theCatch": "Benchmarks are averages, not guarantees, and programs devalue with little or no notice (American, Virgin Atlantic and Qatar all raised prices or fees in 2025-2026), so don't hoard points for years chasing a 'perfect' redemption. The CPP rule also ignores non-cash factors: if you literally can't afford the cash fare, a 'low' CPP redemption can still be the right call. And cash fares earn miles and count toward status; award tickets usually do not.",
      "riskLevel": "low",
      "legal": "Fully legitimate. Comparing cash vs. points and choosing the better value is exactly how loyalty programs are meant to be used; there is nothing an airline or card issuer can penalize here.",
