      "whatItIs": "Airfare is usually cheapest in a mid-range booking window, not as far ahead as possible. Expedia's 2026 Air Hacks report (built on ARC airline ticketing data) found the cheapest domestic economy fares are booked 15-30 days out, and the most expensive are booked 180+ days out. International was cheapest booked either 8-15 days out or 31-45 days out, again beating 180+ days out. Note this partly contradicts the older 'book international 3-5 months ahead' guidance from Google Flights, Hopper, Going and The Points Guy, who still recommend booking international coach 3-5 months out to lock in limited cheap-fare inventory. Both can be true: booking weeks out is cheaper on average but riskier on availability.",
      "saves": "Expedia 2026: domestic economy ~$130 cheaper booked 15-30 days out vs 180+ days out; international ~$190 cheaper booked 31-45 days out vs ~6 months out, and up to ~$225 cheaper booked 8-15 days out ($585 vs $813 at 180+ days). Broader industry guidance (Google Flights/TPG): domestic average cheapest ~43 days (1-2 months) out; international 3-5 months out.",
